WARN mcp/infra PAUSED degraded=0 unavailable=0 updated=2/3
HINT UNAVAILABLE: operator Available is not True, or pool nodes are down outside a rollout: oc describe co/mcp, oc get nodes; do not upgrade until it is resolved
HINT DEGRADED: Degraded=True: oc describe co/<name> for an operator, oc describe mcp plus machine-config-daemon logs for a pool; fix it before the upgrade
HINT BLOCKED: Upgradeable=False blocks minor-version updates (patch updates still run): read the condition message, fix it or give the admin acknowledgement it asks for
HINT STALLED: updated is below machineCount, the pool is not updating and not paused: it is stuck, check nodes for a stale desiredConfig and the machine-config-controller logs
HINT PROGRESSING: an operator is mid-rollout: wait for Progressing=False, or the upgrade stacks a second rollout on top
HINT PAUSED: spec.paused=true: the pool ignores new rendered configs and stays on the old version; unpause before the upgrade unless it is a deliberate canary
RESULT CRIT verdict=NO-GO crit=5 warn=2 operators=10 pools=4 healthy=7
